OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F312A1786324673
OL,3,CWhy is looking directly at a solar
OL,4,Ceclipse dangerous?
OL,6,FImo Bell, a planetarium astronomer at
OL,7,Fthe observatory, said: "It's not a
OL,8,Ftotal eclipse, but over 90% is really
OL,9,Fexciting. We're not going to get one
OL,10,Fthis good for a really long time."
OL,12,FBut why is it dangerous, and how can
OL,13,Fyou view it safely? ITV News explains.
OL,15,FWhy is looking at a solar eclipse
OL,16,Fdangerous?
OL,18,FEye damage can occur without proper
OL,19,Fprotection. The sun's bright rays can
OL,20,Fburn cells in the retina at the back
OL,21,Fof the eye.
OL,26,@oD@XOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/8
