OL,3,CWhy is looking directly at a solar
OL,4,Ceclipse dangerous?
OL,6,FThe retina doesn't have pain
OL,7,Freceptors, so there's no way to feel
OL,8,Fthe damage as it happens. Once the
OL,9,Fcells die, they don't come back.
OL,11,FSymptoms of solar eye damage, called
OL,12,Fsolar retinopathy, include blurred
OL,13,Fvision and colour distortion.
OL,15,FIn a rare case of eclipse eye damage,
OL,16,Fa woman who viewed an eclipse in North
OL,17,FAmerica in 2017 without adequate
OL,18,Fprotection complained of a black spot
OL,19,Fin her vision.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/8
